ExplanationDescriptionTerraform moduleTerragrunt configs <p>This module is for provisioning the ACM certificate required for end-to-end TLS.</p> <p>An ACM certificate is first requested from AWS Certificate Manager via DNS:</p> <pre><code>resource "aws_acm_certificate" "main" {
  domain_name       = "${var.subdomain}.${var.domain_name}"
  validation_method = "DNS"

  tags = {
    Name        = "${var.project_name}-${var.environment}-acm-cert"
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>ACM returns domain validation options (dvo), which are sets of objects.</p> DVO Breakdown <p>Objects are a collection of named attributes that each have their own type. It's a pair of curly braces containing a series of  =  pairs. These can be seperated by a comma, or line-break.. Example:<pre><code>{
  a = "test123"
  b = "test456"
}
</code></pre> <p>These are contained in a <code>set</code> which is a collection of unique values with no secondary identifiers or ordering. They must be the same type.</p> Example:<pre><code>[
  "d",
  "e",
  "f"
]
</code></pre> <p>These are both examples of structural types.</p> <p>The final format of a <code>dvo</code> ACM returns looks like this:</p> dvo format<pre><code>12:15:03.218 STDOUT [acm] terraform: domain_validation_options = toset([
12:15:03.218 STDOUT [acm] terraform:   {
12:15:03.218 STDOUT [acm] terraform:     "domain_name" = "prod.mazharulislam.dev"
12:15:03.218 STDOUT [acm] terraform:     "resource_record_name" = "_7835c2640307344f99a3609672fcef50.prod.mazharulislam.dev."
